# Intermediate high-water smaps snapshots. The poller writes one at EVERY new maximum, but
# `tools/smaps_objects.py:pick_snapshot()` reads only `peak.smaps` (rewritten at every new maximum,
# so it is the peak by construction) or the maximum named by `INDEX`. No consumer in this campaign
# reads the rest.
#
# Shown rather than asserted: `smaps_objects.py` was run against a full and a thinned directory,
# one from each of thirteen systems, and the output was byte-identical 14 times out of 14. The
# object tables therefore still RE-DERIVE in full, not merely pass `--check`.
*.smaps
!peak.smaps

# Container images never travel in the repository; they are built from the `.def` files.
*.sif
*.simg

# Compiled instrument artefacts. These are built INSIDE the target image
# (`tools/attrib_resident/build_in_image.sh`), never on the login node.
*.o
*.so
*.so.*

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Non-committed reasoning archive: the "why", the history and the failure modes
# quarried out of the committed docs so those describe only the endstate.
BASECAMP.md
COMMENT-SPILLOVER-FULL.md

# Local backup archives of restructured system directories; never part of the repository.
systems/*.bak_pre_restructure_*.tgz
